 uncle  in the comics batman literally watched  his parents pass away as a young child a  lot of young adult books feature lost  parents Lara Jean Covey and to all the  boys I've loved before has no mom  Katniss Everdeen in The Hunger Games  lost her dad and her mom became a broken  shell of a person  Katniss was a tough heroine because she  had already been providing for her  family  tragic backstories make heroes stronger  because they've already had to overcome  stuff they grow up quickly and are used  to lost that makes their stories much  more effective to the audience and it  obviously works there are so many  stories that have missing parents but it  is still super sad there have to be  other ways for Disney to give us  conflict some of the characters have  proven that a parent doesn't have to die  for there to be a great story and  sometimes we just want to watch a Disney  movie without tearing up but we aren't  sure Disney is going to change up their  habit anytime soon it's been a pretty  successful strategy so far there's a  reason why they are one of the most  successful movie companies ever we would  still like to see more characters like  Mulan Merida and Moana though if you  love Disney as much as we do leave a red  heart emoji in the comment section down  below and be sure to tell us who your  favorite Disney characters are while  you're at it and that's a wrap  give this video a big thumbs up if you  love Disney movies and be sure to  subscribe to the things for more videos  like this one thanks for watching we'll  see you next time  [Music]

